    {
      "section": "support.faq",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "title": "Before you ask",
        "intro": "What people want to know before they hand over an archive they spent years building.",
        "items": [
          {
            "question": "Which sources can Shelf pull from?",
            "answer": "Bookmarks, LinkedIn saved posts, Instagram collections, X bookmarks and any web page you send it. Your own notes count as a source too, often the most useful one, because that is where the why lives."
          },
          {
            "question": "Do I have to tag everything?",
            "answer": "No. Tagging is the reason most swipe files die. Shelf reads what you saved and takes the note you wrote at the moment you saved it, and that is enough to find it back later."
          },
          {
            "question": "What happens to the archive I already have?",
            "answer": "You import it. The point of Shelf is not to start a sixth silo. It is to make the five you already have searchable from one field."
          },
          {
            "question": "Who can see what I save?",
            "answer": "Only you. A swipe file is competitive material, and a private one is the only kind worth keeping."
          },
          {
            "question": "What will it cost?",
            "answer": "Not settled yet. Shelf is built for people who save professionally, and the price will reflect that rather than chase the free-app crowd. Waitlist members hear it first."
          },
          {
            "question": "When can I use it?",
            "answer": "Shelf is in private testing. The waitlist is in order, and we widen it as fast as the import can keep up."
          }
        ]
      },
